License: Apache License, Version 2.0

Oh My Keymint adapts the public Binder reply contract in an independent Rust
implementation. It does not bundle upstream C++ code or prebuilt binaries.
The software test implementation uses a publicly known RSA test key, a fixed
test CPU ID and dynamically signed key exports. It cannot provide real TEE
keys, biometric authorization or payment authentication.

The Apache License 2.0 is included in AOSP.Apache-license-2.0.txt.

Public RSA test fixture

Source: https://github.com/RustCrypto/RSA
Version: rsa 0.9.10 (tag v0.9.10)
Referenced source: tests/examples/pkcs8/rsa2048-priv.pem
License: MIT OR Apache-2.0; this fixture is distributed under the MIT license.

This is public test material, not a secret or hardware-backed device identity.
The matching public key is derived from the fixture.

